# htpasswd template / instructions
# This file is a template showing how .htpasswd entries should look.
# Do NOT commit real passwords. Generate .htpasswd on the server using htpasswd utility.
# Example command (on the server or local dev machine with apache2-utils):
#   htpasswd -c .htpasswd admin
# After running, .htpasswd will contain lines like:
#   admin:$apr1$randomsalt$hashedpassword

# Placeholder line (do not use in production):
# admin:REPLACE_WITH_HASHED_PASSWORD

# If you cannot run htpasswd, generate manually on an Apache-enabled machine and upload .htpasswd to the site root.
